 **Link:** [Color and Appearance Modeling](14740-color-and-appearance-modeling.md)
 
 ### [Physics and Optical Modeling](15148-physics-and-optical-modeling.md)
-**What it is:** Extends the standard 3DGS representation to handle non-vacuum media and physically consistent surface extraction by modifying the rendering equation or the underlying density field.
-**What sets it apart:** Explicitly models volumetric attenuation and backscatter or reformulates the Gaussian primitive as a continuous attenuation field, unlike surface-focused material decomposition.
-**When to choose:** When modeling light transport in scattering media (e.g., underwater fog) or requiring geometric consistency for surface reconstruction.
